<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Rano</h1><p class="st-meta">1000 CE – 1807 CE (approx.) · capital Rano</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">One of the seven original Hausa states, a small kingdom south of Kano remembered in tradition as a centre of indigo dyeing.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Little is known beyond <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> tradition. Rano is counted among the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hausa-kingdoms">Hausa Bakwai</a>, the seven states said to descend from Bawo, son of the hero <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayajidda">Bayajidda</a> and the queen of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-daura">Daura</a>. It occupied the plain south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kano">Kano</a> and is thought to have emerged around the same time as its neighbours, by the 11th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>In the traditional division of roles among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa states</a>, Rano and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kano">Kano</a> were the 'chiefs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indigo">indigo</a>', known for dyed cloth. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kano-chronicle">Kano Chronicle</a> shows Rano frequently overshadowed by Kano, whose rulers at times treated it as a dependency, and its own king list is poorly recorded.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fulani-war">Fulani jihad</a> Rano was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kano-emirate">Kano Emirate</a> around 1807, and its town became a district seat under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kano">Kano</a>. A separate Rano <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> was created by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kano-state">Kano State</a> in 2019, reviving the old name.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1000 CE – 1807 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:79.60%;width:16.06%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1000 CE – 1807 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Rano</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam and Hausa traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hausa</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/nigeria">Nigeria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Rano</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1404&amp;focus=kingdom-of-rano" aria-label="Kingdom of Rano on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4916 1747 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Rano lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5236 2003L5144 1947M5236 2003L5236 1986"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5144 1947h0M5236 1986h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5236 2003h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5236 2003h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1404&amp;focus=kingdom-of-rano">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

